  note    `begin` turns autocommit off and `commit` and `rollback` end the transaction by `SQLEndTran` and turn it on again, as .NET's `OdbcTransaction` does; pyodbc's default is autocommit off (measured: `autocommit` reads False), a transaction always open, and here each statement commits on its own until `begin`, as .NET and Go do

